            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="1062" n="1028" xml:id="pg1028"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Matthews
                    files, lot 53 D 413: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United Nations Command
                            (Clark) to the
                            Joint Chiefs of Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>operational immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-05-15T21:03:00+09:00">May 15, 1953—9:03
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>C 62442. Ref ZX 36583.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d522-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Harrison has been instrd to meet
                        tomorrow, 16 May, with a view to further clarifying the basic issues of
                        difference.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In view of the curr tactics employed by the Communists it is questionable
                        whether it will be advantageous to meet on the folg 2 or 3 days. The records
                        today, contained in ref msg, give evidence that the Communists have
                        abandoned any attempt to negotiate, for the present, in favor of a
                        propaganda campaign apparently designed to force US to make concessions. It
                        outlines the propaganda themes which they will exploit to the fullest as
                        long as we permit them to use the Pan Mun Jom sounding board for that
                        purpose.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In order to circumvent these tactics, I am authorizing Harrison, at the end of the 16th May
                        session, to rqst a 2 or 3 day recess. If the Communists do not agree to such
                        a recess, I have directed him to agree to meet the next day, and then at an
                        aprop time to inform the Communists that for administrative reasons he is
                        unable to meet as scheduled, and that he will inform them later when he will
                        be prepared to resume meetings.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Such a recess curtails the Communists propaganda and provides time for my
                        recommended course of action designed to bring matters to a head to reach
                        you and obtain your approval. This recommendation should be in your hands
                        tomorrow.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
